Title: Island Games 2025: Jersey women lose 3-1 to Bermuda in opening game
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [], 'Description': [{'Description': 'Jersey’s women footballers have begun their 2025 Island Games campaign with a 3-1 loss to reigning champions Bermuda.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 83}}, {'Description': 'Anita Tavares gave Jersey a sixth minute lead as she shot left-footed into the corner.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 73}}, {'Description': 'Bermuda hit the Jersey bar shortly before half time as both sides had first half penalty appeals turned down.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 95}}, {'Description': 'But the Bermudans equalised when Jaden Masters struck from close range after an hour before taking the lead 14 minutes later when Khyla Brangman converted from the penalty spot.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 166}}, {'Description': 'The 2023 gold medalists added a third goal in stoppage time when Jya Rattaray Smith reacted quickest after a shot came back off the bar to go top of Group B.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 145}}, {'Description': 'Jersey - who missed out on a semi-final place two years ago due to an administrative error - face Shetland Islands on Monday before meeting Isle of Wight in their final group match on Tuesday.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 168}}, {'Description': 'The loss leaves Jersey bottom of their group after Shetland and Isle of Wight drew 2-2 earlier on Sunday.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 99}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Anita Tavares playing for Jersey'}]}
